deckle-kfxgen

This crate is a Rust port of kfxgen (https://github.com/jloutsch/kfxgen) at commit
0bc705d3ec9489417db5112ef8b40e57da938bed. The dump hook in tools/ref/kfxgen_hook runs inside
kfxgen and is covered by this notice too.

    kfxgen
    Copyright (C) 2025-2026 Justin Loutsch
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3.

kfxgen is offered under version 3 of the licence only, not "or any later version". So this
crate and the hook are GPL-3.0-only, while the rest of Deckle is GPL-3.0-or-later. A program
built with this crate can be distributed under version 3. The licence text is the LICENSE file
at the root of the repository.

kfxgen includes a modified subset of kfxlib, from the KFX Input/Output plugins for calibre:

    Copyright (C) 2016-2025 John Howell <jhowell@acm.org>
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.

Parts of this crate follow kfxlib's behaviour as kfxgen uses it: how a decimal is written, the
approximate locations and pages, and the count of `YJ_symbols` entries. The symbol names in
src/generate/standard_symbols.rs are kfxgen's own (kfxgen's NOTICE), not kfxlib's.

src/epub ports rules from calibre 9.18.0 (https://github.com/kovidgoyal/calibre, tag v9.18.0),
how it reads an EPUB into the book view kfxgen is given:

    calibre
    Copyright (C) 2006-2026 Kovid Goyal and the calibre contributors
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.

Files the port follows: src/calibre/ebooks/conversion/plugins/epub_input.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/conversion/plumber.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/base.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/reader.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/polish/upgrade.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/flatcss.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/guide.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/metadata.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/trimmanifest.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/metadata/__init__.py, src/calibre/ebooks/metadata/opf2.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/metadata/opf3.py, src/calibre/utils/date.py,
src/calibre/utils/localization.py and src/calibre/utils/xml_parse.py. The table of two-letter
language codes in src/epub/package.rs is calibre's (`iso639['2to3']` in
resources/localization/iso639.calibre_msgpack, built from the iso-codes package).
